The goal of cancer informatics is to obtain and organize large amounts of data (ie, histology, radiology, etc) in order to be able to formulate hypotheses and make discoveries about basic cancer development and guide physicians in making correct diagnostic and prognostic decisions. <a href="/research/cancer-informatics" class="more-link" target="_self">Continue Reading &rarr;</a></div></div>
						</article><!-- .slides -->
						<article class="image imageid-2 hentry slides ">
							<figure class="slider-image"><a title="Non-human MRI Analysis" href="/research/non-human-mri-analysis" target="_self"><img title="Non-human MRI Analysis" alt="Non-human MRI Analysis" class="wp-post-image" src="https://web.archive.org/web/20200224105019im_/http://drgutman.org/dglab_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/1.png"/></a></figure><div class="entry-container"><header class="entry-header"><h1 class="entry-title"><a title="Non-human MRI Analysis" href="/research/non-human-mri-analysis" target="_self"><span>Non-human MRI Analysis</span></a></h1></header><div class="entry-content">MRI information from Non-human models offers a unique perspective into general neural functioning and allows for a complement of experimental techniques not available in human specimens. <a href="/research/non-human-mri-analysis" class="more-link" target="_self">Continue Reading &rarr;</a></div></div>
						</article><!-- .slides -->
						<article class="image imageid-3 hentry slides ">
							<figure class="slider-image"><a title="NeuroGenomics" href="/research/neurogenomics" target="_self"><img title="NeuroGenomics" alt="NeuroGenomics" class="wp-post-image" src="https://web.archive.org/web/20200224105019im_/http://drgutman.org/dglab_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/2.png"/></a></figure><div class="entry-container"><header class="entry-header"><h1 class="entry-title"><a title="NeuroGenomics" href="/research/neurogenomics" target="_self"><span>NeuroGenomics</span></a></h1></header><div class="entry-content">The use of in-silico methods to identify and measure brain features using various radiological image resources to study pathological development. <a href="/research/neurogenomics" class="more-link" target="_self">Continue Reading &rarr;</a></div></div>
						</article><!-- .slides -->
			</section>
